## System Capabilities

{{#if can_bind_privileged_ports}}
- **Privileged ports (<1024)**: ✓ Available
{{else}}
- **Privileged ports (<1024)**: ✗ Not available — a port below 1024 that you give explicitly cannot be bound. With no port given, a protocol whose well-known port is below 1024 starts on an OS-assigned port instead and says which; tell the user when the port matters to them.
{{/if}}

{{#if has_raw_socket_access}}
- **Raw socket access**: ✓ Available
{{else}}
- **Raw socket access**: ✗ Not available — protocols that need raw sockets or packet capture (link-layer and raw-IP protocols such as arp, icmp and datalink) refuse to start.
{{/if}}
